AGENTS.md:221:When Phase 126 lands on `main`, the ecosystem expands beyond the core compiler into **6 paired repositories (3 Code Targets + 3 Dedicated Ops Orchestrators)** to maintain gate security, 24/7 CI concurrency, and clean git histories:
docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:218:- **Why it works**: Pure Redblue, gate-verified by tests, requiring no root privileges or native compiler.
docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:223:- **Status**: **Strictly gated behind Phase 109 (Native backend feasibility survey).** Do not start until native compilation is decided.
docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:486:   - **`authorss81/rb-apps-ops`**: Dedicated autonomous application runner, end-to-end integration test gates, performance regressions, and package release pipeline.
docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:492:1. **Separation of Powers (Gate Security)**: Coding agents executing in `rbos`, `rb-apps`, or `rb-pkg` must NEVER have write access to `.github/workflows/` or the gate verification scripts (`verify.sh`). The `-ops` repositories hold the evaluation lock, preventing agents from weakening their own gates.
docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:552:  - **Phase 006 Findings §5 & Phase 073 Findings §1**: `give back` inside an `if` block or loop yields a statement value but does not leave the enclosing block; execution falls through to whatever follows. The tree-walker must propagate an unwinding signal (`return_value: Option<Value>`) across statement blocks, halting iterations immediately while preserving `finally` execution.
