docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:707:### Phase 174: Escape Analysis & Scalar Replacement of Aggregates (SRA)
docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:711:  - **Scalar Replacement of Aggregates (SRA)**: The compiler explodes the record into discrete CPU registers (`rax`, `rdx`) or local stack slots, entirely bypassing memory allocation.
docs/FUTURE_ROADMAP_AND_DEFERRED.md:799:- **Why Before Bootstrapping**: This is the ultimate verification gate. The reference Rust compiler (`rb`) and the self-hosted Redblue compiler (`bootstrap/compiler.rb`) must both achieve 100% byte-for-byte pass rates across all 10,000 tests before the Rust compiler is formally retired.
